  "description": "Calculus for the Epsilon symbolic math library. Gradients, directional derivatives, divergence and curl, Hessians, Laplacians and the second-derivative test for functions of several variables, as vectors and matrices of expressions that compile to fast delegates. Exact antiderivatives from a table of integrals, by substitution, by parts, by partial fractions with Hermite's reduction (over the roots of cubic and quartic factors in radicals too), by Bioche's rules and t = tan(x/2) for rational functions of sin and cos, by t = exp(x) and by trigonometric and hyperbolic substitutions for square roots of quadratics. Numeric definite integrals by the tanh-sinh and exp-sinh rules over finite and infinite intervals, split at the singularities, kinks and peaks found in the expression, accurate at singular ends, and with divergent integrals reported instead of returned as numbers.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "Epsilon.Calculus",
